Deployment status

Stockwise-CRM has been deployed as an independent version of Stockwise using a separate GitHub repository, separate Render backend service, separate AWS Amplify frontend app, and a Neon PostgreSQL database branch/project for the CRM version.

Verified online:

Dashboard loads inventory metrics
Products page loads furniture/appliance demo products with unit prices
Customer Orders page loads CRM KPI cards, leads, follow-ups, and customer profiles
Product-based quote form connects products, quantity, discount, delivery fee, and final estimated value
Record Sale workflow loads products
Record Restock workflow loads products and suppliers
Suppliers page loads supplier data
AI Insights page loads inventory insight data
Backend health check returns database connectivity
CORS is restricted to the deployed Amplify frontend domain

The original Stockwise production deployment was not modified by this CRM upgrade.

What this project demonstrates
Backend API design with FastAPI and SQLAlchemy
PostgreSQL data modeling for inventory, sales, suppliers, customers, leads, and activities
Cloud deployment using AWS Amplify, Render, and Neon
Environment-based frontend/backend configuration
Rule-based inventory and pipeline logic
Product-based quote calculation
CRM-style lead and follow-up workflow design
Dashboard UI for operational decision-making
Deployment safety through a separate repo and independent cloud resources